From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 04:34:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: time-stamp the J604 panel's swaps for
 120 Hz

The J604 (MacBook Pro 14-inch, M4) record admits the panel's 120 Hz timing
(PreciseSyncRate 0x78001f, 120.0 Hz), but its swaps go out with the timing
words zeroed: dcp_m4_swap_encode_full() clears the whole record. The
firmware then completes at most one swap per 16.7 ms, so the mode reports
120 Hz while a vsync-locked client measures 60 fps. On the J604, vkmark
with the FIFO present mode runs every scene at exactly 16.667 ms per frame.

The M4 swap record is the 26.6.2 (25G83) one of the J613 v26 backend: the
same size and the same offsets for the ID, masks, background, brightness,
surface, DVA and nullable bytes. That backend documents the timing
words at 0x00, 0x08 and 0x30 (dcp_v26_swap_set_timing()): with all of
them zero, back-to-back swaps on a 120 Hz panel complete about 16.7 ms
apart. The J516C and T6030 records on 14.7 firmware went from 60 to 120
fps by writing the constant 120 in the same words
(dcp_v14_swap_timestamps()). A counter value makes the firmware time out
on the first swap.

Add swap_timestamps to the M4 board record, set it only for the J604,
and write 120 in the three words of a present (primary plane with a
frame and no intent) on such a board. Blanks, upper-plane-only updates
and the idle-cache registration swap keep zero words, byte for byte as
before, and the J713's 60 Hz record is unchanged. The swap_timestamps
parameter (default on) turns the words off again for an A/B measurement.

D003 still declines realtime bandwidth service: the J613 v26 backend
declines it the same way, and Documentation/gpu/apple-dcp-m4.rst keeps it
declined until a PMC bandwidth owner exists.

Not yet measured on the J604 (needs an on-device run).

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
[j604: k610 drm sync: the J604 record is upstream's dcp_m4_profile_j604 in
 dcp-m4-profile.h (Aurora 3cbacbae40), so .swap_timestamps = true goes
 there. Upstream dcp_m4_runtime_swap_full() also serves the external
 T8132 DCP and encodes with dcp_m4_swap_encode_on(); the timing words are
 written for internal-panel presents only (!ext added), so external
 swaps are unchanged. dcp_m4_swap_set_timing() goes after upstream's
 dcp_m4_swap_encode_full() wrapper. Defaults unchanged: swap_timestamps=1
 (0644), J604 only.]
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-frame.h   | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-profile.h |  3 +++
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c       | 11 +++++++++++
 3 files changed, 34 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-frame.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-frame.h
index 34d81f949a..2fa6cc3db1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-frame.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-frame.h
@@ -274,6 +274,26 @@ static inline int dcp_m4_swap_encode_full(void *output, size_t length, u32 swap_
 				     DCP_M4_PANEL_HEIGHT);
 }
 
+/*
+ * The 26.6.2 swap record opens with the presentation timing words of the
+ * 12.x/13.x firmware, at 0x00, 0x08 and 0x30, as dcp_v26_swap_set_timing()
+ * describes for the same record. With all of them zero, the firmware completes
+ * at most one swap per 16.7 ms on a 120 Hz panel. The constant 120 is a target
+ * that is always past, so a swap is shown at the next refresh; counter values
+ * make the firmware time out (dcp_v14_swap_timestamps()). Call after
+ * dcp_m4_swap_encode_on() or _full(), which zero the record.
+ */
+#define DCP_M4_SWAP_TIMESTAMP_VALUE	120
+
+static inline void dcp_m4_swap_set_timing(void *output)
+{
+	u8 *data = output;
+
+	put_unaligned_le64(DCP_M4_SWAP_TIMESTAMP_VALUE, data + 0x00);
+	put_unaligned_le64(DCP_M4_SWAP_TIMESTAMP_VALUE, data + 0x08);
+	put_unaligned_le64(DCP_M4_SWAP_TIMESTAMP_VALUE, data + 0x30);
+}
+
 /* Swap intent that registers surface 0 as the idle-cache surface. */
 #define DCP_M4_SWAP_INTENT_IDLE_CACHE	8
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-profile.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-profile.h
index 9ed1c952f6..47e5aa99b7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-profile.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-profile.h
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ struct dcp_m4_profile {
 	u32 swap_tail;			/* final two bytes */
 	u32 swap_nits;			/* binary64 brightness */
 	u32 swap_intent;		/* swap intent, 0 for a present */
+	bool swap_timestamps;		/* 120 Hz panel: dcp_m4_swap_set_timing() */
 	u32 disabled_color;		/* background with no surface */
 	u16 done_method;		/* swap completion callback */
 	u32 done_size;
@@ -102,6 +103,8 @@ static const struct dcp_m4_profile dcp_m4_profile_j604 = {
 	.swap_intent = 0x17c,
 	.disabled_color = 0xff000000,
 	.done_method = 590, .done_size = 0x730, .open_method = 457,
+	/* 120 Hz panel: without the timing words it presents at 60 Hz. */
+	.swap_timestamps = true,
 	.brightness_max = 600, .brightness_default = 140,
 	.width_mm = 0, .height_mm = 0,
 	.timing = dcp_m4_timing_j604, .timing_elements = 6,
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 62e08871d1..b747b67bf5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -150,6 +150,10 @@ static const struct kernel_param_ops t8132_ext_swap_depth_ops = {
 module_param_cb(t8132_ext_swap_depth, &t8132_ext_swap_depth_ops, &t8132_ext_swap_depth, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(t8132_ext_swap_depth,
 		 "J713 external direct swaps in flight at most, 2 (default) or 1, from the next frame. At 2 a flip event can come before the firmware confirms the frame replaced the previous one, so a compositor may draw into a buffer still on screen; at 1 every flip event comes with its swap's completion");
+static bool swap_timestamps = true;
+module_param(swap_timestamps, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(swap_timestamps,
+		 "J604: stamp presents with the swap timing words so the 120 Hz panel shows them at 120 Hz, not 60 Hz (default: on; applies from the next swap; J713: no effect)");
 
 struct iomfb_m4 {
 	struct apple_dcp *owner;
@@ -2262,6 +2266,13 @@ static int dcp_m4_runtime_swap_full(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r, bool primary,
 	if (!ret)
 		ret = dcp_m4_swap_encode_on(input, DCP_M4_SWAP_SIZE, id, primary, frame, upper,
 					    keep, brightness_change, nits, check, width, height);
+	/*
+	 * Internal panel presents only: a blank, an upper-only update, an
+	 * intent and an external output keep zero words.
+	 */
+	if (!ret && !ext && primary && frame && !intent && dcp_m4_pf->swap_timestamps &&
+	    READ_ONCE(swap_timestamps))
+		dcp_m4_swap_set_timing(input);
 	if (!ret && intent)
 		dcp_m4_swap_set_intent(input, intent, surface_id);
 	if (!ret)
